{"name":"Spaghetti Strap Pink","hex":"#fbaed2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spaghetti","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pasta made in the shape of long thin strings.","A dish that has spaghetti (noun 1 sense 1) as a main part of it, such as spaghetti bolognese."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of spaghetto"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spaghetti"},{"term":"strap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, narrow, pliable strip of leather, cloth, or the like.\n\nA strap worn on the shoulder.","A strap worn on the shoulder."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To beat or chastise with a strap; to whip, to lash.","To fasten or bind with a strap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strap"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spaghetti strap","blocks":[{"text":"A spaghetti strap is a very thin shoulder strap used to support clothing, while providing minimal shoulder straps over otherwise bare shoulders. It is commonly used in garments such as swimwear, camisoles, crop tops, brassieres, sundresses, cocktail dresses, evening gowns and bodycons, so-named for its resemblance to the thin pasta strings called spaghetti."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Black_jacket_017.jpg/330px-Black_jacket_017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spaghetti_strap"},{"title":"Spaghetti","blocks":[{"text":"Spaghetti is a long, thin, solid, cylindrical pasta. It serves as a staple food of Italian cuisine and is made of milled wheat and water, with the standard Italian version using durum-wheat semolina. The pasta is usually white because refined flour is used, but whole wheat flour may be added. Spaghettoni is a thicker form of spaghetti, while spaghettini is a thinner form. Capellini is a very thin spaghetti, while vermicelli is intermediate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Spaghettoni.jpg/330px-Spaghettoni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spaghetti"},{"title":"Strap","blocks":[{"text":"A strap, sometimes also called strop, is an elongated flap or ribbon, usually of leather or other flexible materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Hose_strap_folded.jpg/330px-Hose_strap_folded.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strap"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Drying_Spaghetti_in_Gragnano.jpg/500px-Drying_Spaghetti_in_Gragnano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Drying_Spaghetti_in_Gragnano.jpg/500px-Drying_Spaghetti_in_Gragnano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A rack of drying spaghetti in a factory in Gragnano.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrying_Spaghetti_in_Grag